  "notes_2026_09_10": "Added 18 symbols (12 -> 30) per MEXC-SYMBOL-EXPANSION-TASK.md / MEXC-PAIR-EXPANSION.md: USD1USDT, USD1USDC, GOLD(XAUT)USDT, GOLD(XAUT)USD1, GOLD(XAUT)USDC, SOLUSDC, TAOUSDT, TAOUSDC (Group A/B, wire 5 new USDT-anchored triangles) + PUMPUSDT, ENAUSDT, BNBUSDT, DGAIUSDT, DOGEUSDT, LITUSDT, ETHFIUSDT, BCHUSDT, ADAUSDT, TRXUSDT (Group C, feed/observation only, referenced by no triangle). Re-fetched and re-verified against api.mexc.com/api/v3/exchangeInfo on 2026-09-10: all 18 status=1, isSpotTradingAllowed=true; precisions, per-symbol commissions and PERCENT_PRICE_BY_SIDE bands match the values below. min_notional is the venue-wide 1.0 (quoteAmountPrecision=1 for all). min_qty: exchangeInfo returned baseSizePrecision=0 (no LOT_SIZE filter published) for USD1USDT, USD1USDC, GOLD(XAUT)USD1, GOLD(XAUT)USDC, TAOUSDC, PUMPUSDT, ENAUSDT, DGAIUSDT, LITUSDT, ETHFIUSDT -- for these min_qty is the 10^-base_asset_precision fallback (MEXC-SYMBOL-EXPANSION-TASK.md open item #1 option (a)); SymbolFilterLoader derives qtyStep the same way independently, so this only affects the min-qty floor. SOLUSDC advertises no MARKET order type (like ETHUSDC/XRPUSDC) -- exec.Unwinder.java:198 already gates its MARKET fallback on per-symbol order_types. taker_bps=0.0 on the USDC/USD1 pairs is a MEXC promotion with no announced end date; if it ends those dry-run triangles silently become unprofitable (harmless while dry-run=true, would need a fee refresh before any live cutover).",
  "notes": "Re-fetched 2026-09-07 (cf-arb-bot-review-plan.md second pass / REVIEW.md verification) to add bid_multiplier_up/ask_multiplier_down (PERCENT_PRICE_BY_SIDE) for unwind-price band clamping (Tier A4) and to re-confirm order_types. CORRECTION to this file's previous notes: the prior pass concluded 'IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL is the real MEXC order-type value and no symbol supports it' -- that conclusion was WRONG. MEXC's actual documented type ENUM for POST /api/v3/order is LIMIT / MARKET / LIMIT_MAKER / IOC / FOK (confirmed against MEXC's own published spot v3 API reference, section 'New Order', twice), and there is NO separate timeInForce request parameter -- it does not appear in the request parameter table at all (only in responses). IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL/FILL_OR_KILL are not values this endpoint accepts; IOC/FOK are the real short forms. Separately confirmed live across ALL 2074 MEXC spot symbols (not just these 9-13): order_types is always exactly one of two arrays, [LIMIT,MARKET,LIMIT_MAKER] or [LIMIT,LIMIT_MAKER] -- IOC/FOK never appears in exchangeInfo's per-symbol order_types for ANY symbol on this venue. A strict membership check against order_types can therefore never pass for type=IOC; BotService.validateOrderType treats that combination as unverified-but-permitted (loud startup WARN), not fail-closed, and the credentialed 1-USDT probe remains the real gate before dry-run=false. ETHUSDC/SOLUSDC/XRPUSDC additionally advertise no MARKET at all -- any unwind fallback path that assumes MARKET is universally available is wrong for those three.",
